{"event_type":"review","id":"17c2287a715120508fa9ab223aa33892a07cbc89b949db0481637d5c763862da","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T15:04:54Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/09f2a2939b9d7a3d2cce9261d290b2c87afc39de1fc5e48c250f02a73cfdc1fa","sha256":"09f2a2939b9d7a3d2cce9261d290b2c87afc39de1fc5e48c250f02a73cfdc1fa"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cc21e0398b0265445b14271e7c1ffc69914896dd6bec4b9baf4a476bd9a87892","sha256":"cc21e0398b0265445b14271e7c1ffc69914896dd6bec4b9baf4a476bd9a87892"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ea311c8cd914d3c74d17b7e2f8d3405af2213fc17610b83697de2ee3646dc54c","sha256":"ea311c8cd914d3c74d17b7e2f8d3405af2213fc17610b83697de2ee3646dc54c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9dd87b99c4b1d264572defdf6b0de8eb680cfa96ac5676739aba8550053a6692","sha256":"9dd87b99c4b1d264572defdf6b0de8eb680cfa96ac5676739aba8550053a6692"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b8e1b4b46c236b824e18b541dd8dd0db787c89310d3be40092d25a2669763243","sha256":"b8e1b4b46c236b824e18b541dd8dd0db787c89310d3be40092d25a2669763243"}],"attempt_id":"fd144a6e679d296d83bbe95ec8e74be499b2351bc5acc05a152b72f4e1367b40:0:1","base":"c357088a040537e52441cda2c7f83582c6e30062","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"7e3b5df16f1c4fa6b9c0574c0055dbafa6e11d85","body":"**Report `deferredVendorDebt: 'unknown'` when a leg ran but produced no report.**\n\nLine 841 sets `deferredVendorDebt: 'absent'` on an `exception` row. Lines 923-924 also set `'absent'` for any `result` whose `report` is `undefined`. In both cases the leg was dispatched. It may have created durable author debt before it threw or failed. No report exists to show that it did not. The row then claims that no debt exists without any evidence for that claim.\n\nThe same function already uses `'unknown'` at Line 929 when the head is unattributed. A leg with no evidence should get the same truthful label. The header comment at Line 34 forbids invented attribution, and the same reasoning applies here. `'absent'` is correct only for `not-admitted` rows (Line 854), because those legs never ran.\n\nOverall `status` is not affected. A `failed` or `exception` row already makes the aggregate `failed`. The defect is only in the per-row value that consumers read.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n       rows.push({\n         ...base,\n         status: 'exception',\n         attribution: 'absent',\n         reason: outcome.exception,\n         fixesPerRun: 0,\n-        deferredVendorDebt: 'absent',\n+        deferredVendorDebt: 'unknown',\n       });\n```\n\n```diff\n     const debt: AddressManyRow['deferredVendorDebt'] =\n-      report === undefined\n-        ? 'absent'\n-        : trusted\n+      trusted\n           ? report.deferredVendorDebt === undefined\n             ? 'absent'\n             : 'present'\n           : 'unknown';\n```\n\nIf you want a separate message for a missing report, change the reason at Line 932.\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 922-929","id":"4f1c54ae42de58320aa7efe3e790d8225e0be9de495e4583616cf0707b1aef98","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressManyPlan.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Report `deferredVendorDebt: 'unknown'` when a leg ran but produced no report."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"a4a23b2584259cec3461bc0a7402d1bd7d426b40","body":"**The wrapper drops `limitations` and `advisories` from the per-area plans.**\n\nLines 21-28 build one `ReviewPlan` per area. Line 29 keeps only their `sessions`. Line 50 then returns `original`, which holds the limitations and advisories of the whole-change plan.\n\nAn area plan can enter partition mode and run without tools. In that case `createReviewPlan` pushes a `limitations` entry such as \"partitioned fallback ran without tools\". That entry is lost here. The returned plan then hides a real verification limit of the area sessions that will run.\n\nMerge the area limitations into `original`, deduplicated:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   original.sessions = sessions;\n+  for (const limitation of new Set(plans.flatMap((plan) => plan.limitations)))\n+    if (!original.limitations.includes(limitation)) original.limitations.push(limitation);\n   original.coverage.mode = 'partitioned';\n```\n</details>\n\nArea plans receive only non-excluded components, so exclusion limitations are not duplicated.","id":"3908632e7aac27bf7c75ba6611a48400cc05bd0ffa7d24cb72b139c37dc6c87e","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/areaReviewPlan.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"The wrapper drops `limitations` and `advisories` from the per-area plans."}],"head":"e45f535a2a44a2cbedf7c682c81d2b986935a8d3","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"9b10f5128d65b7a88250f5fbdb84a6223b424bfb","intervals":[[1,97]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts"},{"blob":"3ad3b19856dd807f58981707d34765c4ccb921c0","intervals":[[1,89]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts"},{"blob":"7e3b5df16f1c4fa6b9c0574c0055dbafa6e11d85","intervals":[[1,1004]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressManyPlan.ts"},{"blob":"a4a23b2584259cec3461bc0a7402d1bd7d426b40","intervals":[[1,55]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/areaReviewPlan.ts"},{"blob":"046d82efceef44a07710162bd1f40b9b5c3e2ea2","intervals":[[1,112]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/durableDisposition.ts"},{"blob":"1087f6cab0e3aafe5d47254d8424e58a5b4accd5","intervals":[[1,439]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/reviewAreas.ts"}],"job_id":"fd144a6e679d296d83bbe95ec8e74be499b2351bc5acc05a152b72f4e1367b40:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection",